# Picking up the recipe book by your pillow (#184, the Prologue's Scene 2).
# Played by the RecipeBook prop. You hold it up and it's yours (on your
# toolbar: select it and Use it to read it anywhere); it opens; and when you
# close it, the lantern, low on his table across the room, asks about it.
# The captain calls from up on deck.

~ start
@hold_up recipe_book
set has_recipe_book
narrator: You got the *Recipe Book*! Small, battered, the corners frayed. Select it on your toolbar and *Use* it to read it, wherever you are.
@put_away
@read recipe_book
@shot stove_nook
lantern: What's that?
- (Show him the book) -> shown

~ shown
lantern: A recipe book!
lantern: Are you a cook?
- (Hesitate, then nod) -> a_cook

~ a_cook
set said_a_cook
lantern: Oh!
lantern: Well, that's something!
heron: Come up on deck when you're ready.
@shot free cut
